---
source: crates/trust-cg-test/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help_of(&[])"
---
Repository test, fuzz, and proof workflows behind one CLI. Implemented commands delegate to
maintained script-backed runners; planned commands return an explicit not-implemented status. Use
each subcommand's `--help` for its current requirements and examples. Generic JSON building-block
schemas are committed under `evals/schema/`; command-specific JSON shapes remain unstable in v0.1.0.

# Examples

  trust-cg-test matrix --format human
  trust-cg-test doctor --for fuzz
  trust-cg-test report --out reports/weekly/2026-04-19.md

Usage: trust-cg-test [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  matrix                    WS1 — Run the workspace unit/integration test matrix
  suite                     Planned WS2 llvm-test-suite runner (not implemented in v0.1.0)
  fuzz                      Planned WS3 differential-fuzzing dispatcher (not implemented in v0.1.0)
  rustc                     WS4 — Drive `rustc_codegen_trust_cg` + rustc UI tests
  bootstrap                 Planned WS5 rustc bootstrap driver (not implemented in v0.1.0)
  ecosystem                 Planned WS6 crates.io smoke runner (not implemented in v0.1.0)
  prove                     Planned WS7 AY proof dispatcher (not implemented in v0.1.0)
  pipeline                  Planned WS8 non-ISel proof dispatcher (not implemented in v0.1.0)
  report                    WS9 — Generate weekly report + dashboard
  jit-diagnostic-dashboard  Generate Phase 3 JIT diagnostic dashboard exports from fixtures
  ratchet                   Run ratchet checks (called by CI)
  doctor                    Check environment for required tools
  lint-linux                Cross-compile check for Linux `#[cfg(target_os = "linux")]` paths in
                            `trust-cg-codegen` (issue #346). Safe on macOS-only boxes — targets not
                            installed via `rustup target add` are reported as `skipped`
  help                      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (human, json, junit)

          Possible values:
          - human: Pretty table + narrative, targeted at humans
          - json:  Machine-readable JSON
          - junit: JUnit XML for CI consumers

          [default: human]

  -o, --out <PATH>
          Override the command-specific output file or directory.

          See the selected subcommand's help for its output type and default.

      --timeout <SECS>
          Per-unit timeout in seconds. Subcommands may apply per-unit defaults when this is unset

      --parallel <N>
          Worker count (honors cargo-serialization lock). Default: auto

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress progress bars; errors still go to stderr

  -v, --verbose...
          Show debug-level events. Repeat for more: -vv, -vvv

      --no-cache
          Ignore proof / corpus caches

      --dry-run
          Print what would run without executing external tools

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
